### Page 3 of 3

```text
Clerk note: Audio recording of the meeting was stopped]
Mayor Kaysen reconvened the special meeting at 8:00 p.m. and noted Mr. Shanor (due to a prior
commitment) would not be in attendance for the remainder of the meeting.  Mr. Evans reported the
Union has reached no consensus on the City’s counterproposal at this time and they will work on a
counteroffer to present to the governing body at the next special meeting on March 12, 2015.  Mr.
Bertsch commented generally on professional services provided by fire fighters vs. monetary issues;
Union’s position on retaining one position currently funded through a grant, additional bunker gear
request, specialty teams and pay, and perception and wage parity with other City employees.  He noted
the Union’s intent to continue to work toward an agreement.
Mayor Kaysen advised the purpose of the special meeting had been met, and there being no
further business previously noted for the special meeting, adjourned the meeting at 8:09 p.m.
Submitted by,
Carol Intlekofer, MMC
City Clerk
This notice is available in alternative, accessible formats upon request.
Published:
Wyoming Tribune-Eagle
March 21, 2015
```
